ine, relieves oxidative stress but increases atherogenic lipids in bipolar disorder</article-title><source>Tohoku J Exp Med</source><year>2007</year><volume>213</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>79</fpage><lpage>87</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17785956</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b69-ndt-9-493"><label>69</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Machado-Vieira</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Andreazza</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Viale</surname><given-names>CI</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Oxidative stress parameters in unmedicated and treated bipolar subjects during initial manic episode: a possible role for lithium antioxidant effects</article-title><source>Neurosci Lett</source><year>2007</year><volume>421</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>33</fpage><lpage>36</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17548157</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b70-ndt-9-493"><label>70</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Khairova</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Pawar</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Salvadore</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Effects of lithium on oxidative stress parameters in healthy subjects</article-title><source>Mol Med Rep</source><year>2012</year><volume>5</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>680</fpage><lpage>682</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">22200861</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b71-ndt-9-493"><label>71</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Guloksuz</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Altinbas</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Aktas Cetin</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><etal/></person-gr